# Scripts keep the line endings their shells need, on every checkout and in a downloaded ZIP. cmd.exe wants CRLF in
# a .bat (a label can be missed in an LF one), and bash stops at "set: pipefail: invalid option name" on a .sh that
# was checked out with CRLF (a Windows clone used from WSL or Git Bash). Nothing else is listed: every other file
# follows each machine's own git settings, as before.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sh text eol=lf
